This is the completed read-only diagnostics partition. Its29entries separate production uninstrumented serving, finite benchmark coordination, Torch/CUPTI observation, NCU kernel replay and postcapture CPU analysis. No new profiles, GPU jobs, tests, builds or source edits were performed. Exact sources are hashed; the existing stopped6efcontainer was read with Docker-cp only to resolve the pinned framework exit contract.

The actual6efN24capture and closed6513analysis succeeded with all8source/maps/CUPTI28/positiveCPU+CUDA/retirement/raw-hash proofs. Its37.2instrumented aggregateTPS and historical4efe65.3uninstrumentedTPS have different instrumentation and conditions. The difference is neither an algorithmic gain/loss nor a calibrated overhead correction. CPU project times are profiled wall intervals, not busy CPU time; NCCL activity includes waiting and is not useful GPU utilization.

Finite screens start CPUworkers behind a barrier and acquire real logical permits. They poll scheduler CPUmetadata at nominal100Hz, maintain bounded callback arrays and require actual allNdecode membership plus first delivery before freezing the common10-second interval. Callback IDchecks, timestamps, queue snapshots, progress/stats and thread/GIL coordination can perturb dispatch. None is itself a GPU math kernel or CUDA data readback. Expected cancellation occurs only after endpoints are frozen; Future/backend/permit/Stream retirement is then mandatory and excluded from decodeTPS. CPUarray.tolist and retiredStream.out snapshots are distinguished from GPUtensor.tolist.

Torch capture starts after constructor warmup but before bringup/readiness/cohort/drain, with one profiler in each of8rank processes. It requests CPU+CUDA, allthreads andtrace_only; shapes, stacks and memory profiling are off. Tool-owned RecordFunction wrappers, fixed counters and original-function restoration add CPU instrumentation. They preserve original operations/outcomes but do not have zero overhead. Kineto/CUPTI native buffers, event correlation and driver collection have runtime-managed costs; no exact per-event overhead or shippingTPS adjustment is invented.

The profiler stop fence is sourced exactly. The copied version.py records04cf2557f315a350e7eea7ab064288def65db75a/CUDA12.9, and copied profiler.py SHA48829e86... matches the prior protected receipt. CUDAactivity selects use_device=cuda. This capture does not select the customcupti_monitor backend. stop_trace delegates to autograd.profile.__exit__, whose427–433device_module.synchronize precedes442_disable_profiler. In6ef, engine.close already precedes capture.finish, so this stop/drain/export/source-audit work is outside the frozen decode interval. No broader PyTorch/CUPTI native-internal audit or unknown flush timing is claimed. The official04cfURL and a local5abcheckout were unsuitable exact-source lookups and were not used as proof.

Exports preserve full raw JSON; hashes, bounded streaming summaries, maps/source/CUPTI rechecks and report serialization can consume substantial CPU/I/O after GPUretirement. Actual6efcontains the old unconditionalreader.close failure cut and2GiB/rank reader allowance. Its successful positive capture does not qualify future475primary-preserving close handling or4c75boundary-value release/6GiB-per-rank funding. Those future contracts remain separate;48GiBreader commitment does not bound nativeKineto buffers or export files. No overflow/truncation/failure is converted to success.

NCUis a separate diagnostic region. The pinned ELF is /opt/nvidia/nsight-compute/2025.2.1/ncu with SHAa44ff2c7... and Volta support per the selected tool/actualsmoke contract; the earlier NsightSystems2025.1.3/CUPTI27mismatch is not evidence that thisNCUtool is unsupported. Commands disable config-file inheritance, restrict to application-only, start profiling explicitly, select finite kernels and use kernel replay. Clock-control andcache-control are bothnone: there is no requested locking/flush, but replay/pass/cache behavior is not production equivalence. Sections may require multiple passes; no pass count or internal stall is fabricated.

The smoke/expert operations explicitly synchronize before ending the profiled range. Packed weights and output arrays are copied to CPU and checked bitwise before/after replay; these validation costs are intentionally not shipping work. Report import with --import/--csv/--page raw is CPU-only and launches no additional GPU kernel. Parsed finite counters/units and kernel durations remain component measurements, not end-to-end throughput or TP8attention/NCCL performance.

Original canonical ncu_experts_actual.py generates INT64indices. The separate7af9packaged source converts seeded IDs toINT32 to match production MoEBuffers.pick, and records picks_dtype. Those index-specialized kernel/register/counter variants must remain distinctly labelled. Its APP5635/a7b1actual-weight/synthetic-routing component is not current86cb. A frozen sourceHOLD sayingGPU_UNRUN is not live execution authority; only actual Rootrun receipts decide execution status. This inventory ran no permission or counter probe.

Closed6513analysis starts only after terminal-success capture and an initial Portainer-only lease check. It validates all8source/CUPTI/retirement plus frozen case membership, derives a clock-offset hull with uncertainty and contains the translated window in all actual concurrent generation ranges. Two CPUworkers stream/hash all8raw traces; Root commands additionally use nice19 andCPUaffinity0,1. CPUanalysis must finish and allPIDs retire before P3. Rootmay allow a separate numerical GPUcontrol after the analysis initialguard/workers are live; such overlap is not a performance comparison and never alters the immutable captured trace.

Attribution rejects duplicate runtime correlations, separates CUDAgraph launches from plain/unmatched events, uses CPUuser_annotation only and preserves inclusive/exclusive scopes. Kernel activity/gaps include crossing-boundary intervals, while event counts are start-assigned. JSONcharacter bounds are not byte bounds; runtimeRSS/library costs remain qualified/unknown rather than invented. The Rootexecution queue must prohibit simultaneous TorchCUPTI/NCU profiling or profiler/analysis contamination of uninstrumentedP3.

